From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emil Iliev <emil_iliev1994@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:57:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ext): add a retrofit_generator shim and
 `retrofit_library` macro

retrofit_generator is a SharedPartBuilder (`.retrofit.g.part`, combined
into `.g.dart` by source_gen's combining builder under build_runner), so it
fits the existing shared_part_library flow unchanged: one shim binary that
wraps `retrofitBuilder`, plus a macro shaped like `json_serializable_library`.

The ext lock gains retrofit_generator 10.3.3 (analyzer `>=8.4.1 <15.0.0`,
build `>=4.0.2 <6.0.0`, so it resolves against the current analyzer 14.5.0 /
build 4.0.11 line) and its runtime closure: retrofit 4.10.0, dio 5.11.1 and
dio_web_adapter 2.2.2. Every other locked version is unchanged. dio and
dio_web_adapter depend on each other, so the hub merges them into one SCC
target.

Over an `@RestApi` file that uses a freezed + json model and a
`genericArgumentFactories` envelope from another package, the shim's
`.g.dart` is byte-identical to build_runner 2.16.2's. Gazelle does not emit
the macro yet.

Changelog: `retrofit_library` runs retrofit_generator for `@RestApi` dio clients

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

